  "heading": "\\partial.order:on{X}",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{partial order on }X",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\partial.order:on{X}]\nDeclares: R is \\relation:on{X}\nwhen: X is \\set\nsatisfies:\n. [reflexive]\n  forAll: x \"in\" X\n  then: R(x, x)\n. [antisymmetric]\n  forAll: x, y \"in\" X\n  where:\n  . R(x, y)\n  . R(y, x)\n  then: x = y\n. [transitive]\n  forAll: x, y, z \"in\" X\n  where:\n  . R(x, y)\n  . R(y, z)\n  then: R(x, z)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"partial order on $X?$\"\n. description: \"A partial order on $X$ is a reflexive, antisymmetric, and\n                transitive relation.\"\nId: \"656a5a0a-77e8-42ea-857c-4f7d8eda00ac\"",
